[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-SECTION
TITLE: Public Section

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-SECTION-CONTAINER
TITLE: Section Container

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-83
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The GSSC Website Public Frontend Section Container SHALL place the Section Contents it receives: the Section Header when those Contents include a header, the Section Body, and the Section Resources when those Contents include resources.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Section Container is the placement shell for section data on public pages. Contents are the section data; the Container places them. Each placed element's behavior is a separate requirement. Page assembly and Contents APIs are separate features.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Derived for GSSC5-25. PIRs do not define the section Container. REVIEW_STATUS stays Changed until owner approval.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-25
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-84
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Section Container SHALL fill the width of its page content area, stack the Section Contents it places in a vertical order, apply vertical padding on the Container, and keep internal spacing between the Section Header, Section Body, and Section Resources.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Full-width stacking keeps section Contents readable within the page content area as the viewport resizes. Vertical padding and spacing between Header, Body, and Resources separate those elements without crowding. Page assembly chooses where Containers appear on a page.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-25
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-85
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Section Container SHALL use the white theme token for its background, the gray theme token for its border, and the dark-green theme token for its default text, with a sans-serif typeface.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
White background keeps the section aligned with the outermost shell. Theme tokens keep presentation in the organization palette. A fuller color role map for sections is not set yet beyond these token choices.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-25
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-SECTION-HEADER
TITLE: Section Header

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-86
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Section Header SHALL display the header from the Section Contents when those Contents include a header.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A section header identifies the section when the Contents supply one. Absent headers are omitted. This requirement does not set header wording.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-25
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-87
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Section Header SHALL appear above the Section Body inside the Section Container when the Section Contents include a header.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Leading with the header keeps the section title before the body text.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-25
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-88
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Section Header SHALL use a semibold weight and the dark-green theme token for its text color, at a size one and one-half times the Section Body text size.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Semibold dark-green text at one and one-half times the body size distinguishes the header within the Container. A fuller type scale is not set yet beyond this relative size and token choice.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-25
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-SECTION-BODY
TITLE: Section Body

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-89
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Section Body SHALL display the body from the Section Contents.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Every section's Contents include a body. The Body presents that text in the Container. This requirement does not set body wording.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-25
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-90
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Section Body SHALL appear below the Section Header when a Section Header is present, and otherwise at the start of the Section Contents inside the Section Container.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The body follows the header when a header exists, and starts the Contents when it does not, so reading order stays consistent.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-25
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-91
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Section Body SHALL use a normal weight and the black theme token for its text color.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Normal-weight black text keeps body copy readable on the white Container background and distinct from the dark-green header. A fuller type scale is not set yet beyond this weight and token choice.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-25
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-SECTION-RESOURCES
TITLE: Section Resources

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-92
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Section Resources SHALL present each resource from the Section Contents as a Resource Button when those Contents include resources; selection of a Resource Button SHALL open that resource.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Resources accompany some sections. Equal Resource Buttons that open their targets let the visitor reach related material. This requirement does not set the resource catalog.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-25
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-93
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Section Resources SHALL appear below the Section Body inside the Section Container when the Section Contents include resources; SHALL arrange equal-size Resource Buttons in a horizontal strip starting from the left; when that strip overflows the Section width, SHALL present a looping carousel with Resources Prev and Resources Next controls at the ends of the strip, expand the visible Resource Buttons equally to fill the strip width between those controls, slide animation when the strip moves, and movement of the carousel by Left Arrow, Right Arrow, H, and L while a Resource Button is focused; and when that strip fits within the Section width, SHALL show every Resource Button without carousel controls.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A horizontal strip below the body keeps resources grouped after the section text. Overflow uses a looping carousel with end controls and keyboard movement so every resource stays reachable as the Section width changes. Filling the strip between the controls avoids empty space at the end of the visible row without naming a layout framework.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-25
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-94
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Section Resources strip SHALL present Resource Buttons with shared height using the dark-green theme token for button text and border chrome on the white Container background, and SHALL use the gray theme token for each Resource Button background on hover.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Shared button chrome marks resources as equal controls rather than underline-only links. Gray hover marks each button as activatable. Dark-green tokens keep the strip aligned with the organization palette. A fuller button color role map is not set yet beyond these token choices.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-25
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-SECTION-RESOURCE-BUTTON
TITLE: Resource Button

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-137
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Resource Button SHALL display the resource name from the Section Contents and SHALL open that resource's target when the visitor activates the button.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The button label identifies the resource; activation opens the related material. This requirement does not set the resource catalog.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-25
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-138
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Resource Button SHALL occupy one equal-size slot in the Section Resources horizontal strip and SHALL participate in carousel movement when the strip is a carousel.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Equal slots keep buttons aligned in the strip. Carousel participation keeps overflowing resources reachable.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-25
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-139
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Resource Button SHALL use a shared height with the other Resource Buttons, a normal weight, the dark-green theme token for its text and border, the white theme token for its background, and the gray theme token for its background on hover.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Shared height and dark-green chrome mark each resource as an equal hyperlink button on the white strip. Gray hover marks the control as activatable. A fuller button type scale is not set yet beyond these choices.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-25
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-SECTION-RESOURCES-PREV
TITLE: Resources Prev

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-140
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Resources Prev control SHALL move the Section Resources carousel one step toward earlier resources when activated, wrapping from the first resource to the last.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Prev steps the looping strip backward so every resource stays reachable from the ends of the strip.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-25
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-141
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Resources Prev control SHALL appear at the start of the Section Resources strip when that strip overflows the Section width and is presented as a carousel.
