[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-ERROR
TITLE: Public Error Container

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-ERROR-ELEMENT
TITLE: Error Container

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-95
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Public Frontend Error Container SHALL present Application Error Contents or HTTP Error Contents for the current public error, and present neither when there is no public error.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The Error Container places error Contents on public pages when an error occurs. Application Error Contents and HTTP Error Contents are separate requirements. This requirement does not invent page-specific error copy beyond that container contract.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-24
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PHLR-48
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-96
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Error Container SHALL appear inside the Page Outlet region of the App Root when it presents error Contents, sit at the bottom-right of that region and size to its Contents up to one quarter of the viewport width and one third of the viewport height at small and above, span the full width of the Page Outlet and limit its height to one third of the viewport below small, keep Report and Dismiss on a chrome banner outside the scrollable Contents region, and scroll only that Contents region vertically when those Contents exceed those size limits.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
A compact bottom-right placement keeps the error visible without covering the full page. Width and height caps leave most of the page usable as the viewport resizes. Keeping Report and Dismiss on a non-scrolling banner leaves those actions reachable while long Contents scroll inside the caps.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-24
REVIEW_STATUS: Changed
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PHLR-48
  ROLE: Refines

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-97
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Error Container SHALL use the light-red theme token for its background and the dark-red theme token for its border and default text color.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Light-red and dark-red theme tokens mark the Error Container as an error surface in the same family as Prompt field failure chrome. A fuller error color role map is not set yet beyond these token choices.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-24
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: GSSC-PHLR-48
  ROLE: Refines

