[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-ERROR-APPLICATION-CONTENTS
TITLE: Application Error Contents

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-98
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
When the Error Container presents Application Error Contents, those Contents SHALL display the error name, the error description, and the error reference number, and, when the visitor is a logged-in administrator and debugging information is available, provide that debugging information in a collapsible presentation that starts collapsed.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Application Error Contents tell the visitor which application error occurred and how to refer to it. Collapsed-by-default debugging keeps administrator detail available without crowding the summary. This requirement does not set the name, description, reference format, or debugging payload.
<<<
DERIVED: False
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
