[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-PROMPT-OVERLAY
TITLE: Public Prompt Overlay

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-PROMPT-OVERLAY-ELEMENT
TITLE: Prompt Overlay

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-107
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Public Prompt Overlay SHALL present the current queued form from the Public Frontend Prompt Overlay service while open, omit its presentation when that queue is empty, advance to the next queued form when the current form completes or submits successfully, cancel the current form when the visitor dismisses it, move focus to the first form control when a form opens, and submit the current form when the visitor presses Enter in a field or activates a form submit control.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
No Public Frontend PIR defines a prompt overlay. The overlay is the Container for prompt forms whose Contents the Prompt Overlay service queues. Completing or submitting advances the queue until empty. Dismiss cancels only the current prompt. Focus and Enter submit keep interaction on the form. Contact Overlay remains a separate feature that reuses this overlay. Derived because PIRs do not define this overlay.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Form field modules from GSSC5-27. Contact Overlay product UX is GSSC5-31.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-108
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Public Prompt Overlay SHALL cover the viewport with a backdrop while open, center a contents panel over that backdrop, scroll the panel independently of the page, size that panel to the full viewport below the small breakpoint and to at most three-quarters of the viewport width and height at the small breakpoint and above, and keep that panel within the viewport as the page resizes.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Covering and centering focus the visitor on the prompt form. Independent panel scroll keeps the page behind still. Full-screen below small and a three-quarter cap at small and above fit narrow and wide viewports without naming a layout framework.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Proposed for owner review (GSSC5-27). Width bands stay implementation-agnostic.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-109
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Public Prompt Overlay SHALL use the gray theme token at twenty-five percent opacity for its backdrop, the white theme token for the contents panel background, the dark-green theme token for the panel border and panel text, and the sans-serif theme font.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Theme tokens keep overlay presentation aligned with the organization palette. A fuller color role map for overlays is not set yet beyond these token choices.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Proposed for owner review (GSSC5-27). Gray at 25% opacity is the owner-specified backdrop.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-PROMPT-OVERLAY-DISMISS
TITLE: Dismiss

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-110
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Overlay Dismiss control and Escape key SHALL cancel the current prompt when the visitor activates the Dismiss control or presses Escape.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Dismiss and Escape are the cancel paths for the current queued form. Backdrop activation does not cancel. Overlay Contents and field behavior are separate requirements.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Proposed for owner review (GSSC5-27). No backdrop dismiss.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-111
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Overlay Dismiss control SHALL appear at the top-right of the prompt container.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Top-right placement keeps the close path visible without covering the Prompt Form.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Proposed for owner review (GSSC5-27).
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-112
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Overlay Dismiss control SHALL use the dark-green theme token for its symbol color on a transparent background, rounded corners, the gray theme token for its background on hover, and the sans-serif theme font.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Dark-green on a transparent control keeps Dismiss aligned with panel text. Rounded corners and gray background on hover match other public icon buttons and mark the control as activatable without changing the symbol color. A fuller color role map for overlay controls is not set yet beyond these token choices.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Shared icon-button chrome (rounded corners; gray hover) aligned under GSSC5-25.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: >>>
GSSC5-27
GSSC5-25
<<<
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-PROMPT-FORM
TITLE: Prompt Form

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-113
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Form SHALL hold the Prompt Overlay field modules the Prompt Overlay service configured for the current prompt.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The form holds the field modules of the current queued prompt. The Prompt Form Title is a separate requirement. Each field module's behavior is a separate requirement.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Proposed for owner review (GSSC5-27).
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-114
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Form SHALL arrange its fields in a CSS grid with one column below the small breakpoint and two columns at the small breakpoint and above.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
One column on narrow viewports and two columns from small upward keeps field modules readable without naming a layout framework.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Proposed for owner review (GSSC5-27).
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-115
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Form SHALL inherit the Prompt Overlay font and text color theme tokens.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
The form is a layout host for field modules. It inherits overlay type tokens so field chrome stays consistent until each field paints its own presentation.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Proposed for owner review (GSSC5-27).
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-PROMPT-FORM-TITLE
TITLE: Title

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-134
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Form Title SHALL display the title text the Prompt Overlay service configured for the current prompt.
<<<
