A configured title names the current prompt so the visitor knows which form is open. The Prompt Overlay service supplies that title with the form Contents.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Proposed for owner review (GSSC5-27).
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-135
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Form Title SHALL appear at the start of the prompt container header, opposite the Prompt Overlay Dismiss control.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Placing the title in the header opposite Dismiss gives the title room and keeps Dismiss clear of the form fields.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Proposed for owner review (GSSC5-27).
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-136
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Form Title SHALL use the sans-serif theme font, a medium font weight, and the dark-green theme token for its text color.
