[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-PROMPT-TEXT-FIELD
TITLE: Text

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-116
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Overlay Text field SHALL accept visitor text entry with the input type checking the Prompt Overlay service configured for that field, including email checking when configured as email; obscure entered text when configured as a password; present a multiline entry when configured for long content; show its label; start from the default text value when the Prompt Overlay service configures one; and honor enable and disable from that configuration.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Text is the entry field module for free-form and typed values in a prompt form. Type checking, password obscuring, multiline layout, and an optional default value are configuration of that module. Enable and disable gate interaction without removing the field.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Default value support added for GSSC5-27.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-117
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Overlay Text field SHALL place its label on the top border to the left of the entry and participate in the Prompt Form grid.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Entry-style labels sit on the top border so the field remains compact in the form grid.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Proposed for owner review (GSSC5-27).
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-118
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Overlay Text field SHALL use the dark-green theme token for its border and for an italic label, the white theme token for its fill when enabled and the gray theme token for its fill when disabled, the sans-serif theme font, and the red theme presentation for border, label, and content after failed form validation until the visitor modifies the field.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Shared entry-field chrome keeps Text aligned with other prompt fields. Red after failed validation marks the field until the visitor edits it.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Proposed for owner review (GSSC5-27).
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-PROMPT-SELECT-FIELD
TITLE: Select

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-119
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Overlay Select field SHALL present a switch that toggles a checked or unchecked choice, show its label, start from the default checked state when the Prompt Overlay service configures one, and honor enable and disable from the Prompt Overlay service configuration.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Select is the switch-styled checkbox module for a prompt form. An optional default checked state seeds the switch when the prompt opens. Enable and disable gate interaction without removing the field.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Default value support added for GSSC5-27.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-120
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Overlay Select field SHALL place its label inside the field border and participate in the Prompt Form grid.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Switch-style labels sit inside the border so the control reads as one unit in the form grid.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Proposed for owner review (GSSC5-27).
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-121
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Overlay Select field SHALL use the dark-green theme token for its border and for a normal-weight label, the white theme token for its fill when enabled and the gray theme token for its fill when disabled, the sans-serif theme font, and the red theme presentation for border, label, and content after failed form validation until the visitor modifies the field.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Shared switch-field chrome keeps Select aligned with other prompt fields. Normal-weight labels distinguish switch fields from italic entry labels.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Proposed for owner review (GSSC5-27).
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-PROMPT-OPTIONS-FIELD
TITLE: Options

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-122
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Overlay Options field SHALL present mutually exclusive choices as radio options, show a label for the field and for each choice, start from the default choice when the Prompt Overlay service configures one, and honor enable and disable from the Prompt Overlay service configuration.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Options is the radio-group module for a prompt form. Mutually exclusive choices keep a single selection. An optional default choice seeds the group when the prompt opens. Enable and disable gate interaction without removing the field.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Default value support added for GSSC5-27.
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-123
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Overlay Options field SHALL place its field label on the top border to the left, arrange choice labels with their radio controls, and participate in the Prompt Form grid.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Entry-style field labels and inline choice labels keep Options readable in the form grid.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Proposed for owner review (GSSC5-27).
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-124
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Overlay Options field SHALL use the dark-green theme token for its border and for an italic field label, the white theme token for its fill when enabled and the gray theme token for its fill when disabled, the sans-serif theme font, and the red theme presentation for border, label, and content after failed form validation until the visitor modifies the field.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Shared entry-style chrome keeps Options aligned with other labeled prompt fields. Red after failed validation marks the field until the visitor edits it.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Proposed for owner review (GSSC5-27).
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-PROMPT-BUTTON-FIELD
TITLE: Button

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-125
TITLE: Semantic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Overlay Button field SHALL present an activatable control within the Prompt Form, perform the submit role when the Prompt Overlay service configures it as a submit control, show its label, and honor enable and disable from that configuration.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Button is the activatable control module for a prompt form, including submit when configured. Enable and disable gate interaction without removing the control.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Proposed for owner review (GSSC5-27).
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-126
TITLE: Syntactic
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Overlay Button field SHALL place its label inside the control and participate in the Prompt Form grid.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
An in-control label keeps the Button a single activatable unit in the form grid.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Proposed for owner review (GSSC5-27).
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: GSSC-PLLR-127
TITLE: Lexical
STATEMENT: >>>
The Prompt Overlay Button field SHALL use the dark-green theme token for its border and for a normal-weight label, the white theme token for its fill when enabled and the gray theme token for its fill when disabled or hovered, the sans-serif theme font, and the red theme presentation for border, label, and content after failed form validation until the visitor modifies the field.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Shared control chrome keeps Button aligned with other prompt fields. Gray on hover marks the control as activatable. Red after failed validation marks the control until the visitor interacts again when validation applies.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Proposed for owner review (GSSC5-27).
<<<
DERIVED: True
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
CHANGE_DRIVER: GSSC5-27
REVIEW_STATUS: Approved

